{
  "paraphrased_article": "Princess Märtha Louise of Norway, known for her claims of psychic abilities, is the daughter of one of Europe's longest-reigning kings. Her new husband, Durek Verrett, is an American who identifies as a shaman with six generations of spiritual healers in his family. Their wedding took place on Saturday afternoon in Geiranger, and despite being unconventional by royal standards, crowds gathered along the cloudy streets hoping to see the bride. The 52-year-old princess, who ranks fourth in succession to Norway's throne as the only daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, wed the 49-year-old Verrett in a traditional Church of Norway service at the Hotel Union, a four-star venue situated in a small village near Geiranger fjord. The ceremony drew both royalty and celebrities among its 350 guests. The bride was accompanied by seven bridesmaids, including her teenage daughters Leah and Emma Behn from her previous marriage to Norwegian writer Ari Behn, who passed away after their 2017 divorce. Notable royal attendees included her brother Crown Prince Haakon with his wife Crown Princess Mette-Marit, Sweden's Crown Princess Victoria and Prince Daniel, as well as Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien from the Netherlands. The princess has led an unconventional life for royalty, having proclaimed psychic powers and operated a healing school for ten years where students learned to communicate with angels. In 2022, she announced her withdrawal from official royal responsibilities to focus on business ventures with Verrett and create a clearer separation between their activities and the Norwegian royal family. Verrett markets himself on social media as a 'servant of God' and 'energy activator,' counting Gwyneth Paltrow, founder of Goop, among his prominent clients, referring to her as a 'soul sister.'"
}
```

